.nh
.TH "PB-AUTH-LOGIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-auth-login - Sign in through browser approval on any device


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb auth login [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign in through browser approval on any device

.PP
Print an approval link and open it when a browser is available. Sign in through WorkOS on this or another device and explicitly approve the requesting CLI. No local callback listener or copied token is needed. Interrupted attempts resume securely; the existing account remains active until replacement succeeds.

.PP
Sign-in credentials are stored in the selected local profile for its configured Paperboat server. Account commands use that profile; a missing or rejected session must be repaired with pb auth login before protected resources can be used.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--change-account\fP[=false]
	sign in with another account after browser approval

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for login

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print approval and sign-in states as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-browser\fP[=false]
	print the approval link without opening a browser

.PP
\fB--reauth\fP[=false]
	authenticate the current account again


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-auth(1)\fP
